<section class="section" aria-labelledby="naming">
	<h2 id="naming">How files are named</h2>
	<p class="naming-pattern"><code>id-spatialtype-scale-projection-year.format</code></p>
	<p>For example <code>BE-region-01m-4326-2024.geojson</code>.</p>
	<dl class="definitions">
		<dt>id</dt>
		<dd>Unique code of the unit, for example a <a href="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/overview">NUTS code</a> (2 to 5 characters) or a country code (2 characters).</dd>
		<dt>spatialtype</dt>
		<dd><code>region</code>, <code>label</code> or <code>line</code>.</dd>
		<dt>scale</dt>
		<dd><code>01m</code>, <code>03m</code>, <code>10m</code>, <code>20m</code> or <code>60m</code>: the map scale the data is generalised for (1:1 million to 1:60 million).</dd>
		<dt>projection</dt>
		<dd>4-digit <a href="https://epsg.io/">EPSG code</a>: <code>4326</code>, <code>3035</code> or <code>3857</code>.</dd>
		<dt>year</dt>
		<dd>4-digit year, for example a <a href="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nuts/history">NUTS release year</a>.</dd>
		<dt>format</dt>
		<dd><code>geojson</code></dd>
	</dl>
</section>
		</main>
